menu "Application (headset)"

    config HEADSET_ENABLE_USB
        bool "Enter USOUND at boot (starts the USB device stack)"
        default n
        help
            On the ESP32-S3 the USB-OTG PHY and the built-in USB-Serial/JTAG share
            D+/D-. Starting TinyUSB removes the USJ console until the board is
            re-plugged — and because this image re-takes the PHY about a second
            after every boot, replugging alone does not bring COM4 back: recovery
            is holding BOOT while replugging to reach ROM download mode.

            This is the whole point of the usound profile, so it must eventually be
            y. Leave it n while developing over USJ, and turn it on only with
            someone at the board or once TBD-009 (the UART console bridge) closes.

    menu "Button pins"

        config HEADSET_BTN_PIN_VOL_DOWN
            int "Volume down"
            default 10

        config HEADSET_BTN_PIN_VOL_UP
            int "Volume up"
            default 11

        config HEADSET_BTN_PIN_ACTION
            int "Play/pause, and long-press mode override"
            default 0
            help
                Defaults to GPIO 0, the BOOT button, because it is the one control
                physically present on an S3 devkit and so the only one that can be
                exercised before the enclosure exists. It is RTC-capable, so it also
                serves as the deep-sleep wake source. The other two are placeholders.

    endmenu

endmenu
